  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 200 AM CDT Sun Aug 9 2026\n\nExtreme Heat: As discussed above, it will be a hot week as mid\nlevel heights and 850mb temps slowly increase. We will need to\nmonitor clouds/sprinkle chances again early Monday morning\nhowever not seeing much impact currently. Daily temps look to \nreach the middle to upper 90s across a large portion of the \narea however temps may approach or even exceed 100 degrees in \nthe Joplin/SE Kansas area. Typically the rule of thumb to reach\n100 degrees is that dry vegetation/antecedent conditions are \nneeded (brown grass rule) and this is certainly true in that \narea. Therefore given highs approaching 100, it wont take much \nfor heat indicies to come close to or exceed 105. Therefore the \nhighest confidence for locations to reach heat indicies around \n105 is in the warning area. Locations along the spine of the \nOzark Plateau typically mix out a little more. Guidance \ncontinues to suggest a slightly higher moisture axis around the \nTable Rock Lake/Branson area with potential for heat indicies to\nreach 105+ in that area. Not confident in that but will need to\nmonitor mixing in that area over the next day or two to see if \nthat trend decreases. Additional modifications to the Warning \nand Advisory are certainly possible this week.\n\nThe other factor into the Warning/Advisory decision is the very\nwarm overnight lows. Lows in the lower 80s look to occur across\nportions of the warning area early this week as winds remain\nsteady. This can sometimes be just as impactful as the daytime \nheat indicies. The latest NWS Heat Risk tool shows the entire \narea in the Major category with now a few pixels of the Extreme \ncategory by Tuesday. Heat sensitive groups will need to take \nproper precautions. \n\nWe will need to monitor how fast the ridge breaks down past\nWednesday. Latest ensembles suggest that the ridge may hold on\nfor Thursday and Friday and portions of the area could see heat\nproduct extensions however confidence is low at this time.\n\nRain Chances: As just mentioned, the ridge will be attempting to\nbreak down mid/late week. This would allow for rain chances to\nreturn to the area however the highest chances remain just north\nof the area, closer to shortwave energy. Would expect \nadditional modifications to precip chances depending on the \nplacement/strength of the ridge.",
